# Project repo layout

This file comes from the [copier-claude-project](https://github.com/avcopan/copier-claude-project)
template and is updated by `pixi run copier-update`.
Put project-specific instructions in `CLAUDE.md` instead.

## Layout

| path | Git repo? | what it holds |
|---|---|---|
| `~/proj/{{project_name}}/` (this repo) | yes | Context for Claude: instructions, notes, TODOs, plans, reference files, and `repos.txt` |
| `~/code/{{project_name}}/` | no | Just a parent folder for the code repos |
| `~/code/{{project_name}}/<repo>/` | yes | The code repositories being developed in this project, listed in `repos.txt` |

## Working with the code repos

- Code changes go in the code repos and are committed there, with `git -C ~/code/{{project_name}}/<repo> ...` or after `cd`-ing into the repo.
  Notes, TODOs, and plans go in this repo.
  Never commit files from one repo to another.
- Before working in a code repo, read its `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, and `README.md`, if they exist.
  Claude Code does not load them automatically, since the code repos are outside this directory.
  Follow that repo's own conventions.
  The user decides when to push.
- Keep each code repo's `CLAUDE.md` standalone: it should only say things that hold for anyone who clones that repo on any machine.
  Facts about this workspace (where TODOs live, where sibling repos are cloned, how the repos relate to this project) go in this repo instead.
- If a repo listed in `repos.txt` is missing, ask the user to run `pixi run bootstrap`.
  `pixi run status` shows the state of each repo.
- To add a repo, clone it into `~/code/{{project_name}}/<name>`, add a `<name> <url> [branch]` line to `repos.txt`, and remind the user to commit and push this repo.

## This repo

- It is a Pixi workspace (`pixi.toml`), which can hold dependencies and tasks for running and testing the project's code.
- Template updates go through `pixi run copier-update` (see `~/proj/ref/cop/copier-pixi-templates.md`, section 3, for resolving conflicts).
  Never edit `.copier-answers.yml` by hand.
- The shared reference library is indexed at `~/proj/ref/INDEX.md`.
